{"_doc":"Per letter id (order P, I…VIII, E): words = up to 8 lemma keys of lexicon_en.json for the \"today's words\" card, chosen from that letter's English line by chapter band (P/I–II: A1–A2, III–V: B1, VI–VIII/E: B2–C1; widened by one band only when needed), never repeating a lemma of an earlier letter; nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs only — no names, function words, homograph entries, single letters, capitalised or hyphenated words. spots = [] (plate spots keep their words for this language). phrases = 1–2 expressions copied verbatim from the English line: {t: text, m: message index, ko, en, note_ko, note_en} — ko = Korean translation, en = plain-English paraphrase.","lang":"en","letters":{"p1":{"words":["boy","little","field","good","life","talk"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"a good life","m":0,"ko":"좋은 삶","en":"a good life","note_ko":"a + 형용사 + 명사: ‘좋은 ~’.","note_en":"a + adjective + noun."}]},"p2":{"words":["still","just","father","school"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"just as you were","m":0,"ko":"그때 그대로","en":"just as you were","note_ko":"just as: ‘꼭 ~처럼’.","note_en":"just as: exactly the way."}]},"p3":{"words":["seem","remember"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"it seems that","m":0,"ko":"~인 것 같다","en":"it seems that","note_ko":"짐작을 부드럽게 말할 때.","note_en":"A soft way to say what you think is true."}]},"p4":{"words":["wife","ever","grateful"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"My wife","m":0,"ko":"내 아내","en":"my wife","note_ko":"my + 사람: 가족을 말할 때.","note_en":"my + person, for family."}]},"c1-l1":{"words":["take","say","work","think","thank","time","tell","friend"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"I'm glad","m":0,"ko":"기뻐","en":"I'm glad","note_ko":"I'm glad (that) …: 기쁜 까닭을 뒤에.","note_en":"I'm glad (that) … gives the reason."},{"t":"Thank you","m":1,"ko":"고마워","en":"thank you","note_ko":"가장 흔한 고마움의 말.","note_en":"The most common way to thank someone."}]},"c1-l2":{"words":["thanks","word","doubt","trouble","hope","well","again","escape"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Endless thanks","m":0,"ko":"끝없이 고마워","en":"endless thanks","note_ko":"아주 큰 고마움 (글에서).","note_en":"Very warm thanks (written)."},{"t":"I'm well again now","m":2,"ko":"이제 다 나았어","en":"I'm well again now","note_ko":"well again: 아픈 뒤 다시 괜찮아짐.","note_en":"well again: healthy after an illness."}]},"c1-l3":{"words":["please","hand","show","man","play","people","listen","know"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"By order of","m":0,"ko":"~의 지시에 따라","en":"by order of","note_ko":"공식 글의 첫머리 말투.","note_en":"A formal opening."},{"t":"I remain your servant","m":1,"ko":"삼가 드림","en":"I remain your servant","note_ko":"옛 편지의 맺음말.","note_en":"An old letter closing."}]},"c1-l4":{"words":["dear","send","set","come","fine","leave","old","want"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"Dear Martín","m":0,"ko":"사랑하는 마르틴","en":"Dear Martín","note_ko":"편지의 첫머리.","note_en":"A letter opening."},{"t":"as they come out","m":1,"ko":"나오는 대로","en":"as they come out","note_ko":"as: ‘~하는 대로, ~할 때마다’.","note_en":"as: at the time when."}]},"c1-l5":{"words":["ask","idea","whole","thing","worth","able","wish","see"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"I had no time","m":0,"ko":"시간이 없었어","en":"I had no time","note_ko":"have no time: ‘시간이 없다’.","note_en":"have no time: to be too busy."},{"t":"by the grace of God","m":2,"ko":"하느님 은혜로","en":"by the grace of God","note_ko":"고마운 일을 말할 때.","note_en":"For a blessing."}]},"c1-l6":{"words":["house","need","print","lady","table","chair","spit","oil"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"I don't need","m":0,"ko":"필요 없어","en":"I don't need","note_ko":"don't + 동사: 부정.","note_en":"don't + verb makes it negative."},{"t":"everything else","m":1,"ko":"나머지는 다","en":"everything else","note_ko":"else: ‘그 밖의’.","note_en":"else: other, besides."}]},"c1-l7":{"words":["woman","grave","place","sad","repeat","right"],"spots":[],"phrases":[{"t":"asks me to tell you","m":0,"ko":"너한테 전해 달래","en":"asks me to tell you","note_ko":"ask someone to …: ‘~해 달라고 하다’.","note_en":"ask someone to … : a request passed on."},{"t":"do it","m":1,